questions.scenario:
You are debugging a production issue where payment status updates remain stuck in `PROCESSING` status in the database despite the remote payment gateway throwing a `PaymentException`. Database modifications are unexpectedly committing instead of rolling back. Here is the service snippet:

java
@Service
public class PaymentService {
    @Autowired
    private PaymentRepository paymentRepo;

    public void processPayment(Payment payment) throws PaymentException {
        try {
            executePaymentTransaction(payment);
        } catch (PaymentException e) {
            log.error("Payment execution failed", e);
            throw e;
        }
    }

    @Transactional(rollbackFor = PaymentException.class)
    public void executePaymentTransaction(Payment payment) throws PaymentException {
        paymentRepo.updateStatus(payment.getId(), "PROCESSING");
        callRemoteGateway(payment); // Throws PaymentException on failure
        paymentRepo.updateStatus(payment.getId(), "SUCCESS");
    }
}
